-- statement:
--   The theorem states that the defined proposition MainStatement holds. Work in the polynomial ring P = ℂ[p,s,u,F,J] in five variables over the complex numbers, with x = s² + u³ + p²F and H = x²F − (1 + 2sx)J − p²J² − pu. Let A = P/(H) be the quotient by the principal ideal generated by H. The statement asserts five things together: A is a finitely generated ℂ-algebra; A is an integral domain; the Krull dimension of A equals 4; the polynomial ring A[t] in one variable over A is isomorphic as a ℂ-algebra to the five-variable polynomial ring ℂ[X₁,…,X₅]; and A is not isomorphic as a ℂ-algebra to the four-variable polynomial ring ℂ[X₁,…,X₄]. Thus A would be a ring that is not a polynomial ring in four variables but becomes one after adjoining one more variable, a failure of cancellation over ℂ.
